ce can permit prior support to be reinterpreted during later formation. A global decision conflict is not presumed.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-attributes\",\n        \"S-broadcast\",\n        \"S-base\",\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-commit\",\n        \"S-init\"\n      ],\n      \"participants\": [\n        \"Instance coordinator\",\n        \"Accept recipient\",\n        \"later Prepare sender\"\n      ],\n      \"objects\": [\n        \"Instance.Status\",\n        \"AcceptReply\",\n        \"PrepareReply.Status\"\n      ],\n      \"contexts\": [\n        \"Fixed five-node volatile/thrifty EPaxos\",\n        \"Preaccepted instance receiving matching-ballot Accept followed by higher-ballot Prepare\"\n      ],\n      \"event_paths\": [\n        \"handlePropose -> PreAccept recipients -> disagreeing PreAcceptReply aggregation -> bcastAccept -> handleAccept -> handlePrepare\"\n      ],\n      \"activity_classes\": [\n        \"A1\",\n        \"A2\"\n      ],\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-formation\",\n        \"B-authority\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-state\"\n      ],\n      \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n        \"B-config\": \"Determines recipient and quorum counts for a legal slow-path prefix.\",\n        \"B-wire\": \"Status itself is serialized even though VBallot has an independent omission.\"\n      },\n      \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"preservation\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"Nonstale Accept does retain seq/deps and bal/vbal, so this is not total loss of value information.\",\n        \"Already committed recipients preserve their status and smaller-ballot requests are rejected.\",\n        \"A later Commit can establish COMMITTED; the question concerns the acknowledged interval before Commit.\"\n      ],\n      \"unknowns\": [\n        \"Construct a producer-generated slow-path Accept and show actual acknowledgment and later Prepare response on one history.\",\n 